		(uuid "c1146363-0068-5ecc-b9d9-c5eb6b0e4232")
	)
	(text "Moved from the main board (split S1): the 12 V meter (0x4D) and SPARE_SW meter (0x47) on the Pi's I2C, powered by the Pi's 3.3 V through J1 pin 6; pull-ups only at the\nPi.\nSP_EN (J1 pin 9, between GND pins) comes from the main board's RUN through 100k and a series diode; the 68k here pulls EN low, so SPARE_SW is off when RUN drops, the\ndiode opens or the pigtail is unplugged (fail-off). EN about 2.6 V with RUN up.\nSPARE_SW: limit 3.87-4.42 A (499R), dV/dt 3.3 nF about 12 V/ms. SPARE_ON: unswitched, about 2 A limit. B340A clamps on both outputs. SMBJ12A: servo back-feed clamp on\n+12V, 13.3 V min breakdown (over the 12.35 V worst regulated output), 19.9 V at its 30.2 A rating: under the eFuses' 20 V maximum.\n330 uF + 5 x 22 uF now sit at the converter output, not at the far end of the pigtail: recheck the compensation and measure the loop at the 0R injection point before\nloading.\nThe DVE fallback no longer plugs into J24: this board has no 12 V input, and the old DVE adapter pinout puts 12 V on SCL and SP_EN."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 500 0)
		(effects
